
  Set wtm up in the repository you stand in: where its worktrees go, the branch they start from,
  the .env files each one gets and the commands run when one is created or removed. The settings
  stay on this machine, in the repository's git directory, out of git.

  A first init fills each setting from what it finds: origin's default branch, the .env files and
  their templates, the install command of the package manager, a docker compose file to stop.
  Run again, it sets the repository up again from its settings: each one as it is, every .env file
  it finds listed, only those set up picked. Unattended, a flag changes its setting alone.

  A hook is a command, or JSON for one that runs in a folder or goes on after a failure:
    --on-create '{"cmd": "pnpm db:generate", "cwd": "packages/db"}'
  What runs in each worktree is set up by `wtm run init`.

  Usage:
    wtm-next init [flags]

  Examples:
    # The wizard
    wtm init

    # Unattended, from what wtm finds
    wtm init --yes

    # No .env files, two hooks on create
    wtm init --yes --env-strategy none --on-create "pnpm install" --on-create "make setup"

    # Change one setting of a repository set up already
    wtm init --yes --on-clean "docker compose down"

    # See the plan first, then apply exactly that plan
    wtm init --yes --dry-run
    wtm init --expect-fingerprint <hash>

    # For a script or an agent, with the v2 JSON envelope
    wtm init --yes --output json

  Flags:
        --ask                         Ask again the questions this repository remembers an answer to, to change or forget it
        --base-branch string          The branch new worktrees start from by default
        --base-path string            Where new worktrees go, relative to the repository; outside it keeps the main checkout clean
    -n, --dry-run                     Show the plan and its fingerprint, apply nothing
        --env-file strings            The .env files every new worktree gets
        --env-strategy string         Where a new worktree's .env files come from: a fresh checkout has none of your local ones
        --expect-fingerprint string   Apply only if the facts still have this fingerprint, the one --dry-run printed
    -h, --help                        help for init
        --on-clean stringArray        Commands run in a worktree before it is removed, such as stopping what it started
        --on-create stringArray       Commands run in a worktree once it is created, such as installing its dependencies
        --output string               Output format: text or json (default "text")
    -y, --yes                         Run unattended: no question, no confirmation (each setting as given, else as set up, else as found)

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

